  "design_notes": [
    "Section 7.7 has no Strengths column. Strengths are filled only where the design states them elsewhere: Kerolox Workhorse from the example in section 17.5 (and the Part Card of 14.3), Hydrolox High-Efficiency from its drawback sentence (\"best Isp, but ...\"). The other four engines have none yet.",
    "contracts, facts and failure_modes of Kerolox Workhorse are those of the example in section 17.5. F05 (LEO orbital speed) looks like a placeholder there: the fact bank ties F05 to flight phase F7.",
    "Electric-Pump Mini: \"only for small contracts\" is read as C0 and C1; Appendix A shows it offered in C1. The other engines carry no contracts list because the design does not restrict them.",
    "Hydrolox High-Efficiency: throttle 67-109% is stored as throttle_max 1.09. The table thrust (1,860 / 2,280 kN) matches the real engine at its 109% setting, so Core should treat the table thrust as the maximum, not scale it by 1.09 again.",
    "engine_shutdown is listed for every engine because the failure model (8.4) applies it to engines in general; combustion_instability is specific to Kerolox Giant.",
    "Methalox Full-Flow: \"Testing strongly recommended\" names no test; the engine hot-fire is the engine test of section 6.6."
  ],
